Enhancements for the Ultra Identity Card
This template is already rich, but you can add a few fields and tweaks to boost personalization, motivation, and functionality. For example, include inclusive and identity details (like preferred pronouns) and additional gamification or profile fields. Below are some suggestions, backed by research where possible:
Preferred Pronouns: Add a “Pronouns” field (e.g. she/her/they) for inclusivity. Studies stress that including pronouns in profiles – even in email signatures or dashboards – “has an incredible impact” on making trans and non-binary people feel they belong
cultureamp.com
. (This small step signals respect and helps everyone address each other properly.)
Profile Image & Emoji: You already have a Profile Image and signature emoji, which is great. Research shows profile pictures strongly influence impressions – they can even affect hiring decisions in online marketplaces
informs.org
. Similarly, emojis are “essential features of online self-presentation” that convey identity and group affiliation
frontiersin.org
. In practice, use a clear, representative avatar and a memorable emoji combo to reinforce personality. Cohesive visuals (matching colors, logos, icons) also help: well-designed digital badges and profile graphics (like team logos or color themes) boost recognition and professionalism
