. You might attach hidden IDs or metadata to key fields so other tools can verify them. (This isn’t mandatory, but it mirrors how achievement badges are made verifiable
verifyed.io
.)
Miscellaneous Fun Fields: The optional fields you suggested (snacks, rituals, signature move, etc.) are great for flavor. You could also add “If Lost, Return To” (favorite Slack channel or group page) or “Legacy/Mission Statement” to underscore long-term purpose. Even small touches like a 3-word mantra or favorite emoji combo add personality. As one example, adding favorite pronouns or motifs to visible places (like signatures) has been shown to build an inclusive culture
cultureamp.com
, so these playful fields serve a purpose too.
Implementation Note: If you want an auto-generator, you could build a small app or script that takes a data object (JSON) of all these fields and outputs the Markdown card. For example, a Python script could pull each agent’s details from a database and render this template (or even use a GPT function to format it). Integrating with APIs (like Slack, Git, project trackers) can auto-fill stats (XP, current projects, achievements). This way the profile isn’t static text but a live system – akin to how Ping’s “automated credentials” keep identity data in sync
